WEBVTT

00:00:09.957 --> 00:00:11.223
Dad. Sam.

00:00:11.257 --> 00:00:12.857
This is bigger than you
think. They're everywhere.

00:00:12.891 --> 00:00:14.824
Sam: if this demon killed mom
and jess and dad's closing in,

00:00:14.857 --> 00:00:16.024
We got to help.

00:00:16.058 --> 00:00:17.590
Dad doesn't want our help.

00:00:17.624 --> 00:00:20.957
I'm talking one week here, man,
to get answers, to get revenge.

00:00:20.991 --> 00:00:22.223
You think i didn't respect dad.

00:00:22.257 --> 00:00:23.891
Sorry i brought it up. I respected him.

00:00:23.924 --> 00:00:25.891
No matter what i did,
it was never good enough.

00:00:25.924 --> 00:00:27.590
So what are you saying? That
dad was disappointed in you?

00:00:27.624 --> 00:00:29.257
When we finally do find dad,

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:32.091
I don't know if he's
even gonna want to see me.

00:00:32.124 --> 00:00:33.924
Hey! Dad.

00:00:33.957 --> 00:00:35.091
Hey, boys.

00:00:35.124 --> 00:00:37.290
Hi, sam. Hi, dad.

00:00:37.323 --> 00:00:39.924
Last time we were together,
we had one hell of a fight.

00:00:39.957 --> 00:00:42.424
Yes, sir. It's good to see you again.

00:00:42.457 --> 00:00:44.357
It's been a long time.

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:45.390
Sam!

00:00:45.424 --> 00:00:46.724
Dean: we almost got dad killed.

00:00:46.757 --> 00:00:48.290
They're not gonna stop.
They're gonna try again.

00:00:48.323 --> 00:00:50.024
They're gonna use us to get to him.

00:00:50.058 --> 00:00:51.791
Dad's vulnerable when he's with us.

00:00:51.824 --> 00:00:53.290
I got to be a part of this fight.

00:00:53.323 --> 00:00:54.924
Sammy, this fight is just starting.

00:00:54.957 --> 00:00:57.024
You got to let me go.

00:01:17.357 --> 00:01:18.891
Beth: mr. Elkins?

00:01:21.457 --> 00:01:22.624
Mr. Elkins.

00:01:22.657 --> 00:01:24.724
Would you like another?

00:01:24.757 --> 00:01:27.390
Yeah. Thanks, beth.

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:32.657
I thought they caught the unabomber.

00:01:32.691 --> 00:01:35.891
Yeah, poor mr. Elkins lives
all alone up in the canyon.

00:01:35.924 --> 00:01:38.657
Same seat every day,

00:01:38.691 --> 00:01:40.957
Going through his papers,
making his little notes.

00:01:40.991 --> 00:01:44.257
He's a nice old man. He's just a nut.

00:01:46.924 --> 00:01:48.457
Here you go.

00:02:14.091 --> 00:02:15.357
What'll you have?

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:17.824
Jack all around. Leave the bottle.

00:02:17.857 --> 00:02:20.490
You hungry? We have dinner plans.

00:02:24.691 --> 00:02:27.158
Can i get you something
else, mr. Elkins?

00:03:14.857 --> 00:03:16.991
It's been a while.

00:03:17.024 --> 00:03:19.091
I got to say, you look old.

00:03:19.124 --> 00:03:21.424
What do you want? What do you think?

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:24.924
Damn.

00:03:29.457 --> 00:03:30.724
You can do better than that.

00:03:41.991 --> 00:03:43.524
Come on, come on.

00:04:25.757 --> 00:04:27.091
Nice gun.

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:31.857
Wouldn't do you much good, of course.

00:04:31.891 --> 00:04:34.390
Boys...

00:04:34.424 --> 00:04:36.824
We're eating in tonight.

00:04:57.091 --> 00:04:59.657
All right, dude, not a decent
lead in all of nebraska.

00:04:59.691 --> 00:05:00.891
What do you got?

00:05:00.924 --> 00:05:03.857
Well, i been scanning wyoming,
colorado, south dakota.

00:05:03.891 --> 00:05:06.991
Here
- A woman in iowa fell 10,000 feet from an airplane

00:05:07.024 --> 00:05:08.757
And survived.

00:05:08.791 --> 00:05:10.557
Sounds more like "that's incredible!"

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:12.158
Than "the twilight zone."

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:13.390
Yeah.

00:05:13.424 --> 00:05:16.323
Hey, you know, we could
just keep heading east -

00:05:16.357 --> 00:05:18.557
New york, upstate.

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:20.924
Could stop by and see sarah again. Huh?

00:05:20.957 --> 00:05:23.524
She's a cool chick, man. Smokin'.

00:05:23.557 --> 00:05:27.058
You two seemed pretty
friendly. What do you say?

00:05:27.091 --> 00:05:29.058
Yeah, i don't know. Maybe someday.

00:05:29.091 --> 00:05:31.824
But in the meantime, we got
a lot of work to do, dean,

00:05:31.857 --> 00:05:33.058
And you know that.

00:05:33.091 --> 00:05:34.757
Yeah, you're right.

00:05:34.791 --> 00:05:36.991
What else you got?

00:05:37.024 --> 00:05:38.257
Uh, man in colorado.

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:40.624
Local man by the name of daniel elkins

00:05:40.657 --> 00:05:42.524
Was found mauled in his home.

00:05:42.557 --> 00:05:45.091
Elkins. I know that name.

00:05:45.124 --> 00:05:47.091
Doesn't ring a bell.

00:05:47.124 --> 00:05:49.124
Looks like the cops
don't know what to think.

00:05:49.158 --> 00:05:52.490
At first they said it was
some sort of bear attack,

00:05:52.524 --> 00:05:54.824
And now they found signs of robbery.

00:05:54.857 --> 00:05:56.223
Mm-Hmm.

00:05:56.257 --> 00:05:58.424
Yeah.

00:06:01.924 --> 00:06:03.891
Here. Check it out.

00:06:09.724 --> 00:06:11.557
You think it's the same elkins?

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:13.891
It's a colorado area code.

00:06:51.924 --> 00:06:54.490
Looks like the maid didn't come today.

00:07:00.257 --> 00:07:02.724
Hey, there's salt over
here, right inside the door.

00:07:02.757 --> 00:07:04.991
You mean, like,
protection-Against-Demon salt

00:07:05.024 --> 00:07:06.957
Or "oops, i spilled the popcorn" salt?

00:07:06.991 --> 00:07:08.691
It's clearly a ring.

00:07:13.158 --> 00:07:16.357
You think this guy elkins was a player?

00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:17.457
Definitely.

00:07:26.924 --> 00:07:29.390
That looks a hell of a lot like dad's.

00:07:29.424 --> 00:07:32.857
Except this dates back to the '60s.

00:07:57.791 --> 00:08:00.924
Whatever attacked him, looks
like there was more than one.

00:08:00.957 --> 00:08:03.557
Looks like he put up
a hell of a fight, too.

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:05.957
Yeah.

00:08:32.357 --> 00:08:34.590
Got something?

00:08:36.257 --> 00:08:39.257
I don't know. Some
scratches in the floor.

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:40.590
Death throes maybe?

00:08:40.624 --> 00:08:42.457
Maybe.

00:09:01.624 --> 00:09:03.357
Or maybe a message.

00:09:06.124 --> 00:09:09.490
Look familiar?

00:09:09.524 --> 00:09:11.757
Three letters, six digits -

00:09:11.791 --> 00:09:15.791
The location and combination
of a post office box.

00:09:15.824 --> 00:09:17.124
It's a mail drop.

00:09:17.158 --> 00:09:19.091
That's just the way dad does it.

00:09:37.891 --> 00:09:42.024
"J.W."
- You think? John winchester?

00:09:42.058 --> 00:09:44.058
I don't know. Should we open it?

00:09:48.223 --> 00:09:50.058
Dad?

00:09:52.624 --> 00:09:54.924
Dad, what are you doing
here? Are you all right?

00:09:54.957 --> 00:09:55.991
Yeah, i'm okay.

00:09:56.024 --> 00:09:57.524
Look, i read the news about daniel.

00:09:57.557 --> 00:10:00.158
I got here as fast as i could.

00:10:01.924 --> 00:10:04.357
I saw you two up at his place.

00:10:04.390 --> 00:10:06.158
Why didn't you come in, dad?

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:07.457
You know why.

00:10:07.490 --> 00:10:10.190
Because i had to make sure
you weren't followed...

00:10:10.223 --> 00:10:11.991
By anyone...

00:10:12.024 --> 00:10:13.691
Or anything.

00:10:13.724 --> 00:10:17.058
Nice job of covering
your tracks, by the way.

00:10:17.091 --> 00:10:19.957
Yeah, well, we learned from the best.

00:10:19.991 --> 00:10:22.957
Wait, so you came all the way
out here for this elkins guy?

00:10:22.991 --> 00:10:24.158
Yeah.

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:28.058
He was
- He was a good man.

00:10:28.091 --> 00:10:30.524
He taught me a hell
of a lot about hunting.

00:10:30.557 --> 00:10:34.024
You never mentioned him to us.

00:10:34.058 --> 00:10:36.590
We had a -

00:10:36.624 --> 00:10:39.257
We had kind of a falling out.

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:41.924
I hadn't seen him in years.

00:10:43.791 --> 00:10:45.991
I should look at that.

00:10:54.524 --> 00:10:58.590
"If you're reading
this, i'm already dead."

00:10:58.624 --> 00:11:00.891
That son of a bitch. What is it?

00:11:00.924 --> 00:11:03.223
He had it the whole time. Dad, what?

00:11:03.257 --> 00:11:04.757
When you searched the place,

00:11:04.791 --> 00:11:07.190
Did you see a gun, an
antique, a colt revolver?

00:11:07.223 --> 00:11:08.323
Did you see it?

00:11:08.357 --> 00:11:10.557
Uh, there was an old
case, but it was empty.

00:11:10.590 --> 00:11:12.490
They have it. You mean
whatever killed elkins?

00:11:12.524 --> 00:11:14.390
We got to pick up their trail.

00:11:15.924 --> 00:11:18.891
Wait. You want us to come with you?

00:11:18.924 --> 00:11:21.257
If elkins is telling the truth,
we've got to find this gun.

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:23.757
The gun? Why? Because
it's important, that's why.

00:11:23.791 --> 00:11:26.058
Dad, we don't even know
what these things are yet.

00:11:26.091 --> 00:11:28.091
They were what danny
elkins killed best...

00:11:28.124 --> 00:11:30.257
Vampires.

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:31.290
Vampires?

00:11:31.323 --> 00:11:33.190
I thought there was no such thing.

00:11:33.223 --> 00:11:35.457
You never even mentioned them, dad.

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:37.857
I thought they were extinct.

00:11:37.891 --> 00:11:41.924
I thought elkins and
others had wiped them out.

00:11:45.290 --> 00:11:46.657
I was wrong.

00:11:48.657 --> 00:11:52.024
John: most vampire lore is
crap. A cross won't repel them.

00:11:52.058 --> 00:11:53.490
Sunlight won't kill them

00:11:53.524 --> 00:11:55.857
And neither will a stake to the heart.

00:11:55.891 --> 00:11:58.124
But the bloodlust
- That part's true.

00:11:58.158 --> 00:12:00.457
They need fresh human blood to survive.

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:01.891
They were once people,

00:12:01.924 --> 00:12:05.158
So you won't know it's a
vampire until it's too late.

00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:06.924
All yours, baby.

00:12:13.257 --> 00:12:15.390
What?

00:12:15.424 --> 00:12:17.190
Well, i guess you showed that guy.

00:12:17.223 --> 00:12:19.991
What guy? The guy who bet you
you wouldn't buy that shirt.

00:12:20.024 --> 00:12:22.223
I love this shirt.

00:12:24.891 --> 00:12:26.323
Look out!

00:12:30.691 --> 00:12:32.390
What happened to him?

00:12:32.424 --> 00:12:34.190
Call 911.

00:12:57.954 --> 00:13:00.520
Man: 22, i'm going out there.

00:13:00.554 --> 00:13:02.354
Man #2: copy that.

00:13:07.821 --> 00:13:11.153
Sam, dean, let's go.

00:13:11.187 --> 00:13:12.487
Picked up a police call.

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:13.687
What happened?

00:13:13.721 --> 00:13:16.187
A couple called 911. They
found a body in the street.

00:13:16.220 --> 00:13:18.021
Cops got there. Everyone was missing.

00:13:18.054 --> 00:13:19.253
It's the vampires.

00:13:19.287 --> 00:13:20.687
How do you know?

00:13:20.721 --> 00:13:22.554
Just follow me, okay?

00:13:24.954 --> 00:13:26.687
Vampires.

00:13:26.721 --> 00:13:29.021
It's funny every time i hear it.

00:13:29.054 --> 00:13:31.220
[ Indistinct chatter on police radio ]

00:13:35.187 --> 00:13:37.587
I don't see why we couldn't
have gone over with him.

00:13:37.621 --> 00:13:39.554
Oh, don't tell me it's already starting.

00:13:39.587 --> 00:13:41.687
What's starting?

00:13:41.721 --> 00:13:43.454
What do you got? It was them all right.

00:13:43.487 --> 00:13:45.088
It looks like they're heading west.

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:47.220
We have to double back
to get around that detour.

00:13:47.253 --> 00:13:48.621
How can you be so sure?

00:13:48.654 --> 00:13:50.587
I just want to know we're
going in the right direction.

00:13:50.621 --> 00:13:52.253
We are.

00:13:52.287 --> 00:13:54.187
How do you know?

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:56.253
I found this.

00:13:58.420 --> 00:14:01.554
What is it? A vampire fang?

00:14:01.587 --> 00:14:04.721
No fangs
- Teeth. The second set descends when they attack.

00:14:04.754 --> 00:14:06.420
Any more questions?

00:14:09.654 --> 00:14:11.921
Let's get out of here.
We're losing daylight.

00:14:11.954 --> 00:14:15.721
And, dean, why don't you touch
up your car before you get rust?

00:14:15.754 --> 00:14:17.621
I wouldn't have given you the damn thing

00:14:17.654 --> 00:14:20.253
If i thought you were gonna ruin it.

00:14:27.487 --> 00:14:29.487
Vampires nest in groups of 8 to 10.

00:14:29.520 --> 00:14:31.921
Smaller packs are sent
out to hunt for food.

00:14:31.954 --> 00:14:35.187
Victims are taken to the nest,
where the pack keeps them alive,

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:37.088
Bleeding them for days or weeks.

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:39.787
I wonder if that's what
happened to that 911 couple.

00:14:39.821 --> 00:14:41.787
That's probably what dad's thinking.

00:14:41.821 --> 00:14:46.420
Of course, it would be nice if
he just told us what he thinks.

00:14:46.454 --> 00:14:48.287
<i>So it is starting.</i>

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:51.021
What?

00:14:51.054 --> 00:14:52.921
Sam, we've been looking
for dad all year.

00:14:52.954 --> 00:14:55.287
Now we're not with him for
more than a couple of hours

00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:56.487
And there's static already.

00:14:56.520 --> 00:14:59.253
No.

00:14:59.287 --> 00:15:01.520
Look, i'm happy he's okay, all right,

00:15:01.554 --> 00:15:03.420
And i'm happy that we're
all working together.

00:15:03.454 --> 00:15:05.320
Good.

00:15:05.354 --> 00:15:09.520
It's just the way he treats
us like we're children.

00:15:09.554 --> 00:15:10.988
He barks orders at us, dean.

00:15:11.021 --> 00:15:13.354
He expects us to follow
him without question.

00:15:13.387 --> 00:15:15.687
He keeps us on some
crap need-To-Know deal.

00:15:15.721 --> 00:15:17.654
He does what he does for
a reason. What reason?

00:15:17.687 --> 00:15:18.887
Our job!

00:15:18.921 --> 00:15:20.721
There's no time to argue.
There's no margin for error.

00:15:20.754 --> 00:15:22.220
It's just the way the
old man runs things.

00:15:22.253 --> 00:15:24.120
Yeah, well, maybe that
worked when we were kids,

00:15:24.153 --> 00:15:25.487
But not anymore, all right?

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:27.721
Not after everything you and
i have been through, dean.

00:15:27.754 --> 00:15:30.187
Are you telling me you're cool
with just falling into line

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:31.854
And letting him run the whole show?

00:15:33.420 --> 00:15:37.088
If that's what it takes.

00:16:01.220 --> 00:16:03.320
Have some beer, buddy.

00:16:03.354 --> 00:16:05.554
It'll calm your nerves.

00:16:05.587 --> 00:16:07.021
No, thanks.

00:16:07.054 --> 00:16:08.320
Oh, come on.

00:16:08.354 --> 00:16:10.787
You drink enough, i can
taste it in your blood.

00:16:10.821 --> 00:16:12.520
That's gross.

00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:22.021
Well, how about you, babe?

00:16:30.287 --> 00:16:31.520
Attagirl.

00:16:38.153 --> 00:16:40.387
Bo! Wait for luther.

00:17:02.487 --> 00:17:05.220
I missed you, too, baby.

00:17:05.253 --> 00:17:07.854
We've got presents.

00:17:14.287 --> 00:17:15.721
She looks interesting.

00:17:17.787 --> 00:17:18.787
Hmm.

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:22.654
He doesn't.

00:17:22.687 --> 00:17:24.021
Lock him up.

00:17:26.887 --> 00:17:29.921
On second thought, go
ahead and treat yourself.

00:17:34.988 --> 00:17:38.487
[ Crying ] no!

00:17:38.520 --> 00:17:40.054
There's something else.

00:17:42.021 --> 00:17:43.454
This all theirs?

00:17:43.487 --> 00:17:46.854
No. It's from an old friend of yours...

00:17:46.887 --> 00:17:48.387
Daniel elkins.

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:50.354
I caught his scent.

00:17:50.387 --> 00:17:52.887
I thought i'd surprise you.

00:17:52.921 --> 00:17:54.787
Kate, what did you do?

00:17:54.821 --> 00:17:56.520
I made him suffer.

00:17:56.554 --> 00:17:58.621
You shouldn't have done that.

00:17:58.654 --> 00:18:00.021
There are others like him.

00:18:00.054 --> 00:18:02.054
They'll know the signs
and come looking for us.

00:18:02.088 --> 00:18:03.153
We have to be careful.

00:18:03.187 --> 00:18:04.454
Luther, i did it for you,

00:18:04.487 --> 00:18:05.988
For what he did to your family.

00:18:06.021 --> 00:18:08.021
Revenge isn't worth
much if you end up dead.

00:18:11.220 --> 00:18:12.887
I'm sorry, babe.

00:18:12.921 --> 00:18:15.253
I'm sorry.

00:18:21.153 --> 00:18:23.153
I thought you might like that.

00:18:23.187 --> 00:18:25.921
Looks like it was made
around the time you were born.

00:18:27.954 --> 00:18:29.821
I've seen this before.

00:18:29.854 --> 00:18:32.387
Elkins died with it in his hands.

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:36.320
He should have known better
- Using a gun.

00:18:36.354 --> 00:18:39.721
This is no ordinary gun.

00:18:39.754 --> 00:18:41.887
Yeah, dad. All right, got it.

00:18:41.921 --> 00:18:43.988
Pull off the next exit. Why?

00:18:44.021 --> 00:18:46.054
'Cause dad thinks we
got the vampires' trail.

00:18:46.088 --> 00:18:47.120
How?

00:18:47.153 --> 00:18:49.354
I don't know. He didn't say.

00:19:00.854 --> 00:19:03.420
Oh, crap. Here we go.

00:19:03.454 --> 00:19:05.287
What the hell was that? We need to talk.

00:19:05.320 --> 00:19:06.754
About what? About everything.

00:19:06.787 --> 00:19:09.287
Where we going, dad? What's
the big deal about this gun?

00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:11.387
We can q&a after we
kill all the vampires.

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:13.654
Your brother's right. We
don't have time for this.

00:19:13.687 --> 00:19:16.054
Last we saw you, you said it
was too dangerous to be together.

00:19:16.088 --> 00:19:17.687
Now, out of the blue, you need our help.

00:19:17.721 --> 00:19:20.120
Obviously something big's going
down, and we want to know what!

00:19:20.153 --> 00:19:22.253
Get back in the car. No.

00:19:22.287 --> 00:19:24.520
I said get back in the damn car.

00:19:24.554 --> 00:19:25.921
Yeah, and i said no.

00:19:25.954 --> 00:19:27.621
All right, you made
your point, tough guy.

00:19:27.654 --> 00:19:29.887
Look, we're all tired. We
can talk about this later.

00:19:29.921 --> 00:19:31.187
Sammy, i mean it. Come on.

00:19:31.220 --> 00:19:32.854
This is why i left in the first place.

00:19:32.887 --> 00:19:34.754
What'd you say? You heard me.

00:19:34.787 --> 00:19:35.821
<i>Yeah, you left.</i>

00:19:35.854 --> 00:19:38.287
Your brother and me
- We needed you.

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:40.854
You walked away, sam. You walked away!

00:19:40.887 --> 00:19:43.320
You're the one who said,
"don't come back," dad.

00:19:43.354 --> 00:19:45.621
You're the one who
closed that door, not me!

00:19:45.654 --> 00:19:48.420
You were just pissed off you
couldn't control me anymore!

00:19:48.454 --> 00:19:50.153
Stop it! Stop it! Stop it!

00:19:50.187 --> 00:19:52.187
That's enough!

00:19:53.687 --> 00:19:55.287
That means you, too.

00:20:03.120 --> 00:20:04.687
Terrific.

00:20:27.954 --> 00:20:30.021
Luther: you like to watch, huh?

00:20:30.054 --> 00:20:32.220
Me too.

00:20:34.487 --> 00:20:36.153
Ready, baby?

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:53.721
Are you gonna kill me?

00:20:53.754 --> 00:20:58.187
I'm gonna take you so high
you're never gonna come down.

00:21:36.120 --> 00:21:38.487
Welcome home, baby.

00:21:55.827 --> 00:21:57.427
I know what time it is.

00:21:57.460 --> 00:21:58.927
Get in.

00:22:02.261 --> 00:22:05.328
Dean: son of a bitch.

00:22:05.360 --> 00:22:07.827
So they're really not afraid of the sun?

00:22:07.861 --> 00:22:10.694
No, direct sunlight hurts
like a nasty sunburn.

00:22:10.727 --> 00:22:14.594
The only way to kill
them is by beheading.

00:22:14.627 --> 00:22:18.061
And, yeah, they sleep during the day.

00:22:18.094 --> 00:22:21.493
It doesn't mean they won't wake up.

00:22:21.527 --> 00:22:24.994
So i guess walking right
in's not our best option.

00:22:25.027 --> 00:22:27.894
Actually, that's the plan.

00:22:35.927 --> 00:22:37.527
Dad, i've got an extra
machete if you need one.

00:22:37.560 --> 00:22:41.061
Think i'm okay. Thanks.

00:22:41.094 --> 00:22:43.027
Wow.

00:22:49.694 --> 00:22:52.460
So...

00:22:52.493 --> 00:22:55.161
You boys really want
to know about this colt?

00:22:59.261 --> 00:23:00.794
Yes, sir.

00:23:00.827 --> 00:23:03.261
It's just a story...

00:23:03.294 --> 00:23:06.261
A legend, really.

00:23:06.294 --> 00:23:08.393
Well, i thought it was.

00:23:08.427 --> 00:23:11.393
Never really believed it
until i read daniel's letter.

00:23:11.427 --> 00:23:15.294
Back in 1835, when
halley's comet was overhead,

00:23:15.328 --> 00:23:18.927
The same night those
men died at the alamo,

00:23:18.961 --> 00:23:21.861
They say samuel colt made a gun...

00:23:21.894 --> 00:23:23.161
A special gun.

00:23:23.194 --> 00:23:25.261
He made it for a hunter -

00:23:25.294 --> 00:23:28.660
A man like us, only on horseback.

00:23:28.694 --> 00:23:31.627
The story goes he made 13 bullets.

00:23:31.660 --> 00:23:35.594
This hunter used the
gun a half dozen times

00:23:35.627 --> 00:23:39.927
Before he disappeared,
the gun along with him.

00:23:39.961 --> 00:23:43.427
Somehow, daniel got his hands on it.

00:23:43.460 --> 00:23:45.760
They say -

00:23:45.794 --> 00:23:48.427
They say this gun can kill anything.

00:23:48.460 --> 00:23:51.894
Kill anything, like
supernatural anything?

00:23:53.127 --> 00:23:54.894
Like the demon.

00:23:54.927 --> 00:23:56.760
Yeah, the demon.

00:23:56.794 --> 00:23:59.660
Ever since i picked up its trail,

00:23:59.694 --> 00:24:03.861
I've been looking for a
way to destroy that thing.

00:24:03.894 --> 00:24:07.794
Find the gun...

00:24:07.827 --> 00:24:10.328
We may have it.

00:25:41.994 --> 00:25:43.927
Sam: dean.

00:26:07.861 --> 00:26:09.660
There's more.

00:26:44.627 --> 00:26:47.161
Hey.

00:26:47.194 --> 00:26:49.261
Hey, hey, shh. I'm here to help you.

00:27:01.827 --> 00:27:03.493
John: boys, run!

00:27:04.393 --> 00:27:05.594
Dad!

00:27:13.861 --> 00:27:15.427
Dad?!

00:27:17.760 --> 00:27:19.493
Dad?!

00:27:24.727 --> 00:27:27.027
They won't follow. They'll till tonight.

00:27:27.061 --> 00:27:29.460
Once a vampire gets your
scent, it's for life.

00:27:29.493 --> 00:27:30.694
What do we do now?

00:27:30.727 --> 00:27:32.794
You got to find the
nearest funeral home.

00:27:35.560 --> 00:27:37.961
It shouldn't be taking this long.

00:27:37.994 --> 00:27:40.427
I should go help.

00:27:40.460 --> 00:27:42.827
Dean's got it.

00:27:50.360 --> 00:27:52.194
Sammy.

00:27:53.861 --> 00:27:54.861
Yeah?

00:27:57.794 --> 00:28:00.328
I don't think i ever told you this,

00:28:00.360 --> 00:28:03.594
But the day you were
born, you know what i did?

00:28:03.627 --> 00:28:05.694
No.

00:28:05.727 --> 00:28:08.794
I put 100 bucks into a
savings account for you.

00:28:08.827 --> 00:28:11.427
I did the same thing for your brother.

00:28:14.194 --> 00:28:15.727
It was a college fund.

00:28:18.061 --> 00:28:23.228
And every month, i'd put
in another $100 until...

00:28:25.261 --> 00:28:27.660
Anyway, my point is, sam, that

00:28:29.660 --> 00:28:31.794
This is never the life
that i wanted for you.

00:28:31.827 --> 00:28:34.527
Then why'd you get so mad when i left?

00:28:34.560 --> 00:28:38.061
You got to understand something.

00:28:38.094 --> 00:28:40.660
After your mother passed,

00:28:40.694 --> 00:28:44.527
All i saw was evil, everywhere.

00:28:44.560 --> 00:28:50.094
And all i cared about was
keeping you boys alive.

00:28:50.127 --> 00:28:53.594
I wanted you prepared...

00:28:53.627 --> 00:28:55.127
Ready.

00:28:57.360 --> 00:28:59.961
So somewhere along the line, i, uh

00:29:02.660 --> 00:29:04.660
I stopped being your father.

00:29:04.694 --> 00:29:06.560
And i -

00:29:06.594 --> 00:29:10.261
I became your drill sergeant.

00:29:12.294 --> 00:29:16.094
So when you said you
wanted to go away to school,

00:29:16.127 --> 00:29:19.393
All i could think
about, my only thought,

00:29:19.427 --> 00:29:24.460
Was that you were gonna be alone...

00:29:24.493 --> 00:29:26.427
Vulnerable.

00:29:26.460 --> 00:29:29.261
Sammy, it just -

00:29:29.294 --> 00:29:31.427
It never occurred to me what you wanted.

00:29:33.294 --> 00:29:35.594
I just couldn't accept the fact

00:29:35.627 --> 00:29:38.393
That you and me...

00:29:38.427 --> 00:29:39.594
We're just different.

00:29:41.194 --> 00:29:42.460
What?

00:29:45.727 --> 00:29:47.294
We're not different.

00:29:49.727 --> 00:29:51.861
Not anymore.

00:29:54.660 --> 00:29:57.360
With what happened to mom and jess

00:30:01.127 --> 00:30:03.194
We probably have a lot more in common

00:30:03.228 --> 00:30:05.927
Than just about anyone.

00:30:08.294 --> 00:30:10.660
I guess you're right, son.

00:30:14.393 --> 00:30:16.560
Hey, dad?

00:30:18.760 --> 00:30:20.760
Whatever happened to that college fund?

00:30:22.727 --> 00:30:24.527
Spent it on ammo.

00:30:31.594 --> 00:30:32.961
Whoo!

00:30:32.994 --> 00:30:36.493
Man, there's some heavy security
to protect a bunch of dead guys.

00:30:36.527 --> 00:30:38.694
Did you get it?

00:30:48.161 --> 00:30:51.061
You know what to do.

00:30:59.961 --> 00:31:01.627
Kate: car trouble?

00:31:05.794 --> 00:31:07.994
Let me give you a lift...

00:31:08.027 --> 00:31:09.927
Take you back to my place.

00:31:09.961 --> 00:31:11.061
I'll pass.

00:31:11.094 --> 00:31:13.427
I usually draw the line at necrophilia.

00:31:27.727 --> 00:31:31.360
I don't normally get this
friendly till the second date.

00:31:31.393 --> 00:31:34.427
You know, we could have some fun.

00:31:34.460 --> 00:31:37.627
I always like to make new friends.

00:31:47.527 --> 00:31:50.393
Oh, sorry.

00:31:50.427 --> 00:31:52.827
I never really stay
with a chick that long.

00:31:52.861 --> 00:31:54.161
Definitely not eternity.

00:31:54.194 --> 00:31:55.427
Ugh!

00:31:59.861 --> 00:32:01.861
Damn it.

00:32:03.360 --> 00:32:05.194
Barely even stings.

00:32:05.228 --> 00:32:07.560
Give it time, sweetheart.

00:32:07.594 --> 00:32:09.827
That arrow's soaked in dead man's blood.

00:32:09.861 --> 00:32:12.294
It's like poison to you, isn't it?

00:32:15.560 --> 00:32:16.861
Load her up.

00:32:16.894 --> 00:32:19.294
I'll take care of this one.

00:32:29.951 --> 00:32:31.250
Toss this on the fire.

00:32:31.284 --> 00:32:33.384
Saffron, skunks,
cabbage, and trillium -

00:32:33.417 --> 00:32:35.984
It'll block our scent and
hers until we're ready.

00:32:36.018 --> 00:32:37.817
Stuff stinks. Well, that's the idea.

00:32:37.851 --> 00:32:39.517
Dust your clothes with the ashes

00:32:39.551 --> 00:32:41.817
And you'll stand a chance
of not being detected.

00:32:41.851 --> 00:32:43.484
You sure they'll come after her?

00:32:43.517 --> 00:32:45.651
Yeah. Vampires mate for life.

00:32:45.684 --> 00:32:48.150
She means more to the
leader than the gun.

00:32:48.183 --> 00:32:50.117
But the blood sickness
is gonna wear off soon,

00:32:50.150 --> 00:32:51.584
So you don't have a lot of time.

00:32:51.617 --> 00:32:53.083
Half-Hour ought to do it.

00:32:53.117 --> 00:32:55.884
And then i want you out of
the area as fast as you can.

00:32:55.918 --> 00:32:57.117
But -

00:32:57.150 --> 00:32:58.717
You can't take care
of them all yourself.

00:32:58.751 --> 00:33:01.083
I'll have her and the colt.

00:33:01.117 --> 00:33:04.617
But after, we're gonna meet up, right?

00:33:04.651 --> 00:33:08.250
Use the gun together, right?

00:33:10.150 --> 00:33:12.517
You're leaving again, aren't you?

00:33:14.684 --> 00:33:18.150
You still want to go
after the demon alone?

00:33:18.183 --> 00:33:19.651
You know, i don't get you.

00:33:19.684 --> 00:33:22.250
You can't treat us like this. Like what?

00:33:22.284 --> 00:33:23.450
Like children.

00:33:23.484 --> 00:33:26.617
You are my children. I'm
trying to keep you safe.

00:33:26.651 --> 00:33:29.450
Dad, all due respect, but
that's a bunch of crap.

00:33:30.384 --> 00:33:32.517
Excuse me?

00:33:32.551 --> 00:33:34.584
You know what sammy
and i have been hunting.

00:33:34.617 --> 00:33:36.884
Hell, you sent us on a
few hunting trips yourself.

00:33:36.918 --> 00:33:39.050
You can't be that worried
about keeping us safe.

00:33:39.083 --> 00:33:40.617
It's not the same thing, de.

00:33:40.651 --> 00:33:41.751
Then what is it?

00:33:41.784 --> 00:33:43.817
Why do you want us out of the big fight?

00:33:43.851 --> 00:33:45.684
This demon...

00:33:45.717 --> 00:33:48.851
It's a bad son of a bitch.

00:33:48.884 --> 00:33:50.417
I can't make the same moves

00:33:50.450 --> 00:33:52.751
If i'm worried about keeping you alive.

00:33:52.784 --> 00:33:53.951
You can't be as reckless.

00:33:53.984 --> 00:33:55.384
Look...

00:33:55.417 --> 00:33:58.984
I don't expect to make it out
of this fight in one piece.

00:34:01.183 --> 00:34:04.617
Your mother's death...

00:34:04.651 --> 00:34:06.250
It almost killed me.

00:34:07.884 --> 00:34:11.751
I can't watch my children die, too.

00:34:11.784 --> 00:34:12.918
I won't.

00:34:12.951 --> 00:34:14.984
What happens if you die?

00:34:15.018 --> 00:34:16.984
Dad, what happens if you die

00:34:17.018 --> 00:34:19.484
And we could have done
something about it?

00:34:19.517 --> 00:34:20.751
You know, i've been thinking.

00:34:20.784 --> 00:34:22.651
I think maybe sammy's
right about this one.

00:34:22.684 --> 00:34:24.317
I think we should do this together.

00:34:26.584 --> 00:34:29.183
We're stronger as a family,
dad. We just are. You know it.

00:34:30.651 --> 00:34:32.250
We're running out of time.

00:34:33.684 --> 00:34:36.350
You do your job, and
you get out of the area.

00:34:37.584 --> 00:34:39.517
That's an order.

00:34:49.484 --> 00:34:51.684
Is there any sign of those three?

00:34:51.717 --> 00:34:53.651
No. Something else.

00:34:53.684 --> 00:34:55.751
What? Luther, they cut off hank's head.

00:34:55.784 --> 00:34:57.851
And kate?

00:34:57.884 --> 00:35:00.884
I don't know. She wasn't there.

00:35:02.350 --> 00:35:04.018
What are we gonna do?

00:35:09.317 --> 00:35:11.884
It's just a truck up on the highway.

00:35:16.984 --> 00:35:19.417
Kate.

00:35:19.450 --> 00:35:21.717
She's in that truck.

00:36:21.851 --> 00:36:23.284
Boo.

00:36:39.450 --> 00:36:41.684
I told you i'd come back.

00:37:00.450 --> 00:37:02.551
Luther: get out!

00:37:06.784 --> 00:37:08.018
Who are you?

00:37:08.050 --> 00:37:09.384
The name's winchester.

00:37:09.417 --> 00:37:10.851
Where are your friends?

00:37:10.884 --> 00:37:12.450
Cleaning out your nest.

00:37:14.784 --> 00:37:16.484
Where's kate?

00:37:16.517 --> 00:37:18.651
Come here, sweetheart.

00:37:26.250 --> 00:37:28.183
Kate, you all right?

00:37:30.083 --> 00:37:32.317
Dead man's blood.

00:37:32.350 --> 00:37:34.384
You son of a bitch.

00:37:34.417 --> 00:37:38.083
I want the colt
- Elkins' gun.

00:37:38.117 --> 00:37:39.117
Trade.

00:37:39.150 --> 00:37:40.517
Is that what this is all about?

00:37:40.551 --> 00:37:42.350
I mean, you can't shoot us all, right?

00:37:42.384 --> 00:37:43.817
We'll kill you.

00:37:43.851 --> 00:37:46.484
Oh, i don't need it for you.

00:37:46.517 --> 00:37:49.484
I'm saving it for something else.

00:37:49.517 --> 00:37:53.083
Now, put the colt
down or she goes first.

00:37:53.117 --> 00:37:55.717
All right.

00:37:55.751 --> 00:37:58.018
Just don't hurt her.

00:38:05.350 --> 00:38:06.617
Back up.

00:38:08.784 --> 00:38:10.150
Further.

00:38:22.050 --> 00:38:24.551
That's a nice move. You almost made it.

00:38:49.150 --> 00:38:50.183
Ugh!

00:38:54.651 --> 00:38:57.150
Don't! I'll break his neck.

00:38:57.183 --> 00:38:58.851
Put the blade down.

00:39:12.117 --> 00:39:14.717
You people.

00:39:14.751 --> 00:39:16.751
Why can't you just leave us alone?

00:39:16.784 --> 00:39:19.083
We have as much right to live as you do.

00:39:19.117 --> 00:39:20.651
John: i don't think so.

00:39:47.217 --> 00:39:49.884
Luther!

00:40:05.018 --> 00:40:07.117
Kate, don't!

00:40:30.984 --> 00:40:32.984
So, boys...

00:40:37.283 --> 00:40:38.951
Yes, sir?

00:40:38.984 --> 00:40:41.517
You ignored a direct order back there.

00:40:41.550 --> 00:40:43.917
Yes, sir. But we saved your ass.

00:40:49.218 --> 00:40:50.617
You're right.

00:40:50.650 --> 00:40:52.951
I am?

00:40:52.984 --> 00:40:55.350
It scares the hell out of me.

00:40:55.383 --> 00:40:57.250
You two are all i've got.

00:40:59.151 --> 00:41:02.884
But i guess we are stronger as a family.

00:41:02.917 --> 00:41:05.584
So...

00:41:05.617 --> 00:41:09.283
We go after this damn thing...

00:41:09.317 --> 00:41:11.250
Together.

00:41:11.283 --> 00:41:13.517
Yes, sir.Yes, sir.



00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.000
